    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Logistic-SuSiE approximations along the set-size axis: full grid\"\nsubtitle: \"CAVI-Q2 vs gIBSS-Q2 vs gIBSS-Laplace vs global-JJ vs score (experiment 022, n=1000, L=5, 200 reps)\"\nengine: jupyter\njupyter: python3\nexecute:\n  fig-dpi: 110\n---\n\n\nFive logistic-SuSiE arms, all in the Gaussian family $\\mathcal{Q}_2$ (see the\n[pilot](results.qmd) for the arm definitions). Design: sparse 0/1 columns ($n = 1000$,\n$p = 256$, adjacent-column $\\phi = 0.8$), $b_0 = -2$, $L^* = 3$ causals at gap 8 (binary\n$\\phi \\approx 0.47$ between causals) or 64 ($\\phi \\approx 0.05$), fit with $L = 5$. Axis:\nexpected set size $m$, with $\\beta$ calibrated per $m$ to $E[\\text{LRT}] = T$ so detectability\nis matched and only the shape of each feature's likelihood changes with $m$.\n\nAll CS metrics are over **declared** CSs (component $\\log \\text{BF} \\ge 2$). An undeclared\ncomponent has $\\alpha$ near uniform and a 95% set of ~240 of 256 features, so its coverage is\n1 by construction; pooling it in would erase every difference. The ranking of the arms is the\nsame at every $\\log \\text{BF}$ cut from 0 to 10.\n\n::: {#status .cell execution_count=2}\n022-laplace: 24 signal cells x 5 arms, 200-200 reps per cell; 6 null cells.\n:::\n\n\n# Headline: pooled over m {#sec-pooled}\n\n::: {#tab-pooled .cell execution_count=3}\nCAVI-Q2 in absolute terms; every other arm as **arm minus CAVI-Q2** on the same replicates. *coverage*: fraction of declared CSs containing a causal. *size*: median declared-CS size with its interquartile range. *power*: mean over reps of the fraction of the 3 causals captured by a declared CS. *CS/fit*: declared CSs per fit. 95% CIs resample replicates (the independent unit; CSs within a fit are not), jointly for both arms of a difference.\n\n| T | gap | arm | coverage [95% CI] | size (IQR) | power [95% CI] | CS/fit |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 8 | 8 | CAVI-Q2 | 0.898 [0.881, 0.914] | 4 (2-7) | 0.448 [0.431, 0.465] | 1